# AGP — Match HUD Supply icon

Create one production-ready, small HUD icon representing the player's Supply
resource in Urkaaaz. It will visually identify the Supply gauge beside the
unit deployment controls.

## Asset

- Filename: `match_hud_supply_icon.png`
- Format: PNG with true transparency (RGBA)
- Canvas: square, 256 × 256 px
- Intended display size: approximately 48 × 48 dp as the Supply gauge icon
- Keep the complete silhouette inside the central 88% of the canvas, with
  balanced transparent padding on every side.

## Visual direction

Use the attached crate image as the visual reference for a supply crate filled
with field provisions. Create a simpler, instantly readable version: a sturdy
wooden crate with a few clearly shaped supplies, restrained bronze-gold corner
bands, and one warm ivory-gold highlight. The image should communicate stored
provisions available for deploying units, not a purchasable currency.

Match the Urkaaaz match HUD's restrained fantasy style: dark warm wood,
blackened bronze, and muted amber-gold details. Use approximately `#EFDCAF`
for the brightest highlight and `#E1C177` for restrained gold accents. Keep
the crate silhouette and contrast clear when reduced to 48 × 48 dp. Prefer
solid, chunky forms over fine line work, texture, or small decoration.

The icon will sit behind a live Supply counter, in the same way the Mana
counter is rendered over the Mana orb. Keep a broad, dark, uncluttered wooden
area across the center/front face of the crate so an ivory `current/maximum`
value remains legible when rendered over it. Treat the counter as a separate
UI overlay, centered on the icon: do not draw digits into the PNG.

The icon must remain visually distinct from the blue Mana orb, ammunition
icons, unit portraits, and the Send Wave command icon. It should read as the
Supply resource marker, with the live amount/capacity counter overlaid on it.

## Do not include

- Any background, panel, badge, circle, border, frame, shadow, or glow.
- Text, letters, numbers, currency symbols, labels, logos, or faction marks.
- A blue orb, potion, gemstone, coin, ammunition, weapon, or character.
- Detailed scenery, tiny marks, thin outlines, gradients, noise, or realistic
  photographic rendering.
- Any extra interface element or mockup.

## Acceptance checks

1. The transparent PNG contains only the standalone Supply icon.
2. The silhouette reads as stored provisions or deployment supplies at
   48 × 48 dp.
3. Its warm palette distinguishes it from Mana and ammunition at a glance.
4. The central crate face is dark and visually calm enough to support a live
   ivory `current/maximum` counter centered over it.
5. The image is centered, fully visible, and not cropped.
6. The asset contains no text or unintended background.

## Output and review

Return exactly one PNG with the filename, dimensions, and alpha transparency
specified above. Save it for review under:

```text
assets_src/match/hud/
```

Show the icon at its intended HUD size against both the existing dark panel
and a bright background, with a separate sample `20/20` overlay centered on
the crate to demonstrate legibility. Keep that sample out of the delivered
PNG. The user-approved supplied artwork is integrated as the 256 × 256 source
asset and Android drawable; Android renders the live counter at the icon's
center and retains the surrounding Supply progress ring.
